  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ohio federal contract obligations totaled $66.4M for FY2027 to date. The state recorded 439 awards with an average award size of $151K. Obligations fell 99.2% year over year. Annual history shows large swings: FY22 obligations were $7.8B, FY23 obligations were $10.1B, FY24 obligations were $9B, FY25 obligations were $9.8B, and FY26 obligations were $8.1B. The FY2027 total so far is $66.4M, which is a small fraction of prior full fiscal years. The concentration of current-year dollars is uneven across agencies and industries. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $51.9M in FY2027 to date, while other agencies range from $4.5M down to $140K. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing are the top industries in FY2027 to date, with $16.4M and $10.8M respectively. The top vendors in FY2027 to date include LC FLUHARTY CONSTRUCTION LLC with $14.9M and CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC with $10.1M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall so sharply year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 99.2% year over year. FY26 obligations were $8.1B compared with FY2027 to date obligations of $66.4M. The FY2027 to date total represents a much smaller level of spending than each full prior fiscal year: FY22 $7.8B, FY23 $10.1B, FY24 $9B, and FY25 $9.8B. The current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries are concentrating FY2027 spending in Ohio?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $51.9M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice obligated $4.5M and the Department of the Treasury obligated $3.1M, with other top buyers ranging down to $140K. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry in FY2027 to date with $16.4M, followed by Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing with $10.8M, and Security Guards and Patrol Services with $3.9M. Top vendors include LC FLUHARTY CONSTRUCTION LLC with $14.9M and CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC with $10.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Ohio?",
      "a": "Ohio received $66.4M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state recorded 439 awards with an average award size of $151K, and obligations fell 99.2% year over year. Prior full fiscal years were much larger: FY22 $7.8B, FY23 $10.1B, FY24 $9B, FY25 $9.8B, and FY26 $8.1B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Ohio?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs awards the most contracts in Ohio for FY2027 to date, obligating $51.9M. Other top buying agencies in FY2027 to date include the Department of Justice with $4.5M and the Department of the Treasury with $3.1M, with the General Services Administration and NASA each at $2.3M."
